---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Pre"
  description="Privacy Policy for Pre, the sport-specific prehab app."
>
  <main style="background-color: var(--color-bg); min-height: 100svh;">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="mb-8 inline-block text-sm font-medium"
          style="color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body);"
        >&larr; Back to Pre</a>
        <h1
          class="mb-4 font-sans text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl"
          style="color: var(--color-text);"
        >Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm" style="color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body);">
          Effective date: May 21, 2026
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-prose" style="font-family: var(--font-body); color: var(--color-text);">

        <p>
          Your data is yours, not ours. Pre asks you for some sensitive things — what you train for,
          how your body feels, what you've been through — so it can build prehab sessions that actually
          fit you. We take that seriously. This page lays out, in plain language, what we collect, why
          we collect it, who we share it with, and what you can do about all of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pre is made by Borcsik Richárd e.v. — a sole proprietor (egyéni vállalkozó) registered in
          Hungary at 1022 Budapest, Tapolcsányi utca 10, Hungary — which we call "TrainStack" here
          ("we", "us"). We're the data controller for the information described on this page; you can
          reach us at <a href="mailto:privacy@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">privacy@trypre.app</a>.
          Throughout this policy, "you" means anyone using the Pre app or the trypre.app website. We
          don't sell your personal data, and we never share it for advertising.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
        <p>
          Our rule of thumb is simple: we collect only what we need to make Pre work for you. Here's
          what that looks like in practice.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some of this — your sports, body-region ratings, training context, and session feedback — is
          needed for Pre to build your sessions. Without it, parts of the app won't work.
        </p>

        <h3>Your account</h3>
        <p>
          When you sign up, we collect your email address and a display name. If you use Sign in with
          Apple or Google, we receive the basic profile information you authorize through them. That's
          it — enough to give you an account and let you sign back in.
        </p>

        <h3>Your health and fitness details</h3>
        <p>
          This is the heart of what makes Pre useful, and it's the most personal data we hold. You
          tell us, and we keep:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sport types</strong> — the activities you train for</li>
          <li><strong>Body-region capacity ratings</strong> — your own sense of how much you trust each region, like a knee, shoulder, hip, or back</li>
          <li><strong>Training context</strong> — how often and how hard you train, and what equipment you have</li>
          <li><strong>Session history</strong> — what you completed, how long it took, and the feedback you gave us</li>
          <li><strong>Coach chat messages</strong> — what you type to the AI Coach during intake</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          All of this is sensitive, and we treat it that way. It is never used for advertising, and
          it is never sold.
        </p>

        <h3>How you use the app</h3>
        <p>
          We collect a modest amount of usage data to keep Pre working well and to fix what's broken:
          your device type, the app version you're on, which features you use, and crash reports. We
          use PostHog for this. It helps us see where people get stuck and where the app falls over.
          We and our analytics provider also automatically collect your IP address, the rough
          (city-level) location it points to, and device identifiers. And we use your subscription
          status and purchase identifiers — which come to us through RevenueCat and Apple — to unlock
          and manage your paid features. We don't collect precise GPS location.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use your data</h2>
        <p>Everything we collect goes toward a short list of jobs:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Building your sessions</strong> — your capacity ratings, sports, training context, and history are what your personalized prehab guides are built from</li>
          <li><strong>Making the guidance better</strong> — anonymized, aggregate patterns help us sharpen our recommendations over time</li>
          <li><strong>Running your account</strong> — signing you in, managing your subscription, and helping you when you write to support</li>
          <li><strong>Keeping you in the loop</strong> — session reminders, account notices, and the occasional important update. We don't send marketing unless you've opted in</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How AI fits in</h2>
        <p>
          To generate your sessions and Coach replies, we send your health and fitness data to AI
          providers — currently Google (Gemini), OpenAI, and Anthropic, including through OpenRouter,
          which routes requests to these models. They process your data to produce your guides, and how
          they handle it is governed by their own terms. We'll keep this list current as our providers
          change.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because Pre leans on AI, it's worth being clear about what that guidance is and isn't. Please
          read our <a href="/health-disclaimer" style="color: var(--color-accent);">Health Disclaimer</a> —
          Pre is not medical advice.
        </p>

        <h2>The legal basis for your health data</h2>
        <p>
          For the health and fitness data and Coach messages we use to generate your personalized
          sessions, we rely on your explicit consent (under Article 6(1)(a) and Article 9(2)(a) of the
          GDPR and UK GDPR, where they apply to you). You give this consent when you set up Pre and
          start sharing your information. You can withdraw it at any time by deleting your account or by
          emailing us at
          <a href="mailto:privacy@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">privacy@trypre.app</a> —
          but because your health and fitness data is the very thing Pre uses to work, withdrawing your
          consent means we can no longer provide Pre to you, so we'll close your account and delete your
          data as described in 'How long we keep it'.
        </p>

        <h2>Other legal bases we rely on</h2>
        <p>
          Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, we rely on a few other lawful bases for the rest of the
          data we process:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contract</strong> — to create and run your account, sign you in, make paid features available, check your subscription status, and give you the service and support you ask for</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — to keep Pre secure, prevent fraud and abuse, debug problems, keep things reliable, and understand how the app and site are used, in privacy-protective ways that don't override your rights</li>
          <li><strong>Consent</strong> — for non-essential analytics cookies and any marketing messages where the law requires opt-in</li>
          <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — to keep required records and meet tax, accounting, legal, and regulatory requirements</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we keep your data safe</h2>
        <p>
          Your data lives in an encrypted PostgreSQL database hosted by Neon, and our app servers run
          on Google Cloud Run. Neon encrypts your data at rest with AES-256, and everything moving
          between you, us, and our providers is encrypted in transit with TLS. Access is limited to the
          people who need it to do their jobs, and no further. No system is perfectly secure, but we
          hold ourselves to industry-standard practices and keep working at it.
        </p>

        <h2>When we share your data</h2>
        <p>
          We don't sell your personal data, and we don't share it for advertising. We share it in only
          two situations:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>With service providers who help us run Pre</strong> — database hosting (Neon), app and server hosting (Google Cloud), AI session and Coach generation (Google Gemini, OpenAI, and Anthropic — including through OpenRouter, which routes requests to AI models), product analytics (PostHog), payments (Apple App Store), and subscription management (RevenueCat). Each is bound by terms that limit how they can use your data</li>
          <li><strong>When the law requires it</strong> — to comply with a valid legal request, or to protect our rights, our users, or the public</li>
          <li><strong>In a business transfer</strong> — if TrainStack is part of a merger, acquisition, financing, or sale of assets, your data may move with the rest of the business. We'll require whoever receives it to honor this policy, or we'll let you know before anything material changes</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We hold your data for as long as your account is active. If you delete your account, we delete
          your personal data within 30 days — except for the narrow cases where the law requires us to
          keep something longer. We may keep de-identified or aggregated data — information that can't
          reasonably be traced back to you — to understand how Pre performs and to improve it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights over your data</h2>
        <p>It's your data, so you get to decide what happens to it. You can:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access it</strong> — ask for a copy of what we hold about you</li>
          <li><strong>Correct it</strong> — fix anything that's wrong, in the app or by writing to us</li>
          <li><strong>Delete it</strong> — ask us to remove your account and the data tied to it</li>
          <li><strong>Export it</strong> — get your data in a portable format</li>
          <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — take back the consent you gave us to use your health and fitness data; because that data is what Pre runs on, this means closing your account (see 'How long we keep it')</li>
          <li><strong>Restrict</strong> — in some cases, ask us to limit how we use your data</li>
          <li><strong>Object</strong> — object to processing we base on our legitimate interests, and opt out of marketing any time</li>
          <li><strong>Complain</strong> — if you're in the EEA or UK, you can lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these, email us at
          <a href="mailto:privacy@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">privacy@trypre.app</a>.
          We may need to verify your identity first. We'll respond within the time the law requires —
          usually within one month under the GDPR and UK GDPR, and within 45 days under California law,
          with extensions only where they're allowed.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Pre is built for adults. You must be 18 or older to use it, and we don't knowingly collect
          data from anyone under 18. If you believe someone under 18 has given us their information,
          write to us at <a href="mailto:privacy@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">privacy@trypre.app</a> and we'll delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          The trypre.app website uses essential cookies to sign you in and keep your session going. Our
          analytics provider, PostHog, sets first-party cookies so we can understand how the site is
          used. We don't run third-party advertising cookies, and we don't track you across other
          sites. Where the law requires it, we'll ask for your consent before setting non-essential
          analytics cookies, and you can change your choice at any time.
        </p>

        <h2>California privacy rights</h2>
        <p>
          If you're a California resident, you have rights under the CCPA/CPRA: to know the categories
          of personal information we collect and why, to access and delete it, to correct it, and not to
          be discriminated against for exercising those rights. We do not sell or share your personal
          information as those terms are defined under California law, and we do not use or disclose your
          sensitive personal information for anything beyond providing the services you ask for and other
          purposes the law permits. To exercise these rights, email
          <a href="mailto:privacy@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">privacy@trypre.app</a>.
          The categories of personal information we collect, where it comes from, why we use it, and
          the categories of third parties we share it with are described in the 'What we collect and
          why' and 'When we share your data' sections above — together they're our notice at
          collection — and we keep each category for the periods described in 'How long we keep it'.
        </p>

        <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
        <p>
          Your data is processed in the United States. If you're using Pre from the EEA, the UK, or
          elsewhere, we transfer your data to the US relying on approved safeguards where required — such
          as the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, the UK Extension to it, or the European Commission's
          Standard Contractual Clauses with the UK Addendum, as applicable. You can ask us for a copy of
          the relevant safeguard by emailing
          <a href="mailto:privacy@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">privacy@trypre.app</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy now and then. If we change something that matters, we'll tell you in
          the app or by email. The effective date at the top always reflects the current version.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          If anything here is unclear, or you just want to know more about how we handle your data,
          write to us at
          <a href="mailto:privacy@trypre.app" style="color: var(--color-accent);">privacy@trypre.app</a>.
          A real person will read it.
        </p>

      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .legal-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-prose ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-prose li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal-prose a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
